   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Dark Star** (1 other source): Performed in a style similar to Big River [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **It Must Have Been The Roses**: rare: 7 archived performances [10]\n- **Half Step**: back after 234 archived shows (2567 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [10]\n- **Lovelight**: rare: 9 archived performances [10]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2023-06-27.aud.mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 195 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **dac2023-06-27.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: source not stated; 21 songs; 195 min; rated 3.5/5 by 6 [2]. Said about its sound: Audio cuts out abruptly before the song concludes; File transitions directly into Half Step without missing audio content [8][9]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Listener attended with son and girlfriend, marking their first show together [6]\n- Listener previously saw the band nineteen times in the 1990s, including six at Deer Creek [6]\n- Band started hot, dipped in energy during the second set, then recovered after drums [7]\n- Mortgage lender joke delivered on stage regarding venue naming rights [7]\n- Mickey and Oteil played Drums, with Jay returning for the next song [2]\n- Band remained on stage before Touch of Grey due to time constraints [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2023-06-27.aud.mp3**: taped by Dave Mason; transferred by Dave Mason; source: AUD [1]. Also: Microphones attached to hat brim recorded from lawn between rows E and F [1]\n- **dac2023-06-27.AKGmix.toaste.flac16**: taped by Toaste; transferred by Toaste; source: Center Lawn near Front > 1x AKG d222e cardioid (C); 1x AKG394 figure-8 (L,R); 2x AKG 391 cardioids (L,R); 2x AKG392 omnis 2-foot spread (L,R); 2x AKG398… [2]",
